# Bugs of the prototype (Nov 2004 debug build; the code matches the GameCube SHA1) in the shooting gallery (room r22c),
# fixed as the final game does them (US retail disc, st2_4.rel, compared instruction by instruction). A user's report
# of 20.11.2026: "the order of the enemies does not change. It does not progress beyond 5 targets, even if you achieve
# a score of 4500". Decision of the project owner 22.10.2026: prototype bugs the final game does not have are fixed.
# - The second game (type B) came only in levels A and B and only with caps of other levels (A: caps 9 and 10, B: 14
#   and 17); the final game plays it in every level once three of that level's five caps are owned.
# - The sixth (special) cap of a level was the item number 0xF0..0xF3 used as a cap number: cap[0xEF] was written past
#   the work and item 0x1CB given, so it never came; and only in the second game. The final game gives cap 21..24
#   (items 0xF0..0xF3) when not owned yet, for 4000 points or more, or more than 24 hits without hitting the Ashley
#   target, in either game (the Ashley target's hits counted at work 0x48, as there).
# - A set (the bonus at six caps) was six caps in a row (A's set needed one of B's); the final game counts the level's
#   five caps and its special one, the case grid's row.
# - Debug leftovers the final game does not have: "GIVE UP: (X) button" (X ended the game at once, before its
#   targets came), X held at the start (level select), L+R+Y (all 24 caps), L held or a jump point at the room's entry
#   (level D / B / C). Hits count only while the game runs (step 2), as there.
# - The castle's second way in (from r31d) offered only game A; the final game offers all four, as from r305 (the
#   room's init already had r31d).
